# Build-time public configuration for the web app.
#
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* belongs here — everything in this file is compiled into
# the client bundle and is world-readable. Real deployments override these.
#
# NODE_ENV is deliberately absent: `next build` sets it to production itself,
# and injecting NODE_ENV=development from the shared .env silently broke the
# build for weeks with a misleading "<Html> should not be imported" error.
#
# These are LOCAL-PREVIEW fallbacks only (`next build && next start` on this
# machine). A real deployment MUST set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL and
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL as build-time environment variables on the host, which
# take precedence over this file.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUILD time, not read at runtime. Setting it only
# in the host's runtime environment has no effect — the bundle would ship with
# whatever was present when `next build` ran. On Vercel this means the two
# variables must exist in Project Settings BEFORE the build, and changing them
# requires a redeploy, not a restart.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
